message: "If you use this software or its generated benchmark artifacts, please cite this release."
type: software
title: "Trustworthy ADMET Benchmark: Reliability Regret after Single-Metric Random-Resplit Validation Selection"
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21374237
repository-code: "https://github.com/huajianv587/admet-trustworthy-benchmark"
authors:
  - family-names: Jiang
    given-names: Huajian
    affiliation: "College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS), Nanyang Technological University, 50 Nanyang Avenue, Singapore 639798, Singapore"
    email: jian0157@e.ntu.edu.sg
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-3992-2286"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible code, configurations, de-identified prediction views, and
  audit outputs for a 22-endpoint, five-model, five-seed study of reliability
  after random-resplit validation-only ADMET model selection on fixed TDC
  held-out test partitions. The release includes dimension-specific
  candidate-pool comparisons
  and zero-refit selected-model analyses of Morgan-support risk--coverage and
  validation-fitted calibration. Selected-model Morgan-support ordering was
  favorable versus random on 20 of 22 endpoints but generally weaker than
  ensemble uncertainty; selected-only isotonic mapping improved ECE on 9 of 13
  endpoint means and Brier score on 7 of 13. These are post-hoc descriptive
  sensitivities. Morgan support/error rank association is a support-score
  informativeness measure, not an accuracy or reliability oracle.
keywords:
  - ADMET
  - QSAR
  - model selection
  - calibration
  - uncertainty quantification
  - Morgan fingerprint support
  - risk-coverage
  - molecular machine learning
